<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert the Strong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/866">866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert the Strong was a Frankish count and margrave of Neustria under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, charged with defending the lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretons">Bretons</a>. He was killed fighting them at Brissarthe in 866. His sons Odo and Robert I both became kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a>, and he was the ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robertians">Robertians</a> and of the Capetian kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-the-strong.jpg" alt="Robert the Strong" width="245" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%A9n%C3%A9alogie_des_rois_de_France_-_Besan%C3%A7on_Ms677_f139v_Robert_le_Fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
